        "title": "Oral Tradition: Memory, Performance, and Transmission - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Literate cultures assume text is the primary form of communication — documents are produced, preserved, copied, and read. Oral cultures existed for 300,000 years of Homo sapiens before writing, and most human languages have never been written. The study of oral tradition reconstructs:"
    },
    {
